🚀 **Day 56/60: Complete Your MVP & Deploy a Live App | Claude AI Coding Challenge**

Today marked one of the most rewarding milestones of the challenge—turning an AI project into a **working, live Minimum Viable Product (MVP)**.

Instead of adding more features, the focus shifted to what truly matters before launch:
✅ Reviewing the entire codebase for stability and integration
✅ Ensuring every core feature works seamlessly together
✅ Testing the complete end-to-end user journey
✅ Identifying and fixing production-specific issues
✅ Updating documentation and cleaning up the GitHub repository
✅ Deploying the application to a free hosting platform for the world to access

A great MVP isn't about having every feature—it's about delivering a reliable product that solves a real problem and is ready for users.

One of the biggest takeaways from today's challenge was seeing how **Claude AI** acts like an experienced technical lead—reviewing code, spotting issues before deployment, suggesting improvements, and helping prepare a production-ready release.

🎉 By the end of Day 56, the project wasn't just running on my local machine—it was **live, accessible, and ready to be shared with anyone through a web browser.**

Building software is exciting, but **deploying something real that people can use is where the real learning begins.**

Only **4 days** remain in this incredible 60-day journey, and it's exciting to see how an idea has evolved into a deployable AI application.

